cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Urban Heat Island — Łódź: vegetation, built-up land and summer surface heat from Landsat"
message: "If you use this software, data or study, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arzimanli
    given-names: Suad
    affiliation: "University of Łódź"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/suadarzimanli/urban-heat-island-lodz"
url: "https://suadarzimanli.github.io/urban-heat-island-lodz/"
keywords:
  - urban heat island
  - land surface temperature
  - NDVI
  - Landsat
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - Łódź
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible analysis and interactive web map of summer surface heat in
  Łódź, Poland. Landsat 8/9 land surface temperature and NDVI from twenty clear
  summer days (2018–2025) on a 500 m grid, with ESA WorldCover built-up share;
  regression checked by spatially blocked cross-validation, Moran's I, and
  Getis–Ord Gi* hot and cold spots. Vegetation explains about 90% of the
  spatial pattern of surface heat; the residual pattern shows a historic centre
  cooler than expected and industrial sites and the airport hotter.
